{"link":{"rel":"self","url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/6442d8a2d34ee8d4ade8e6db"},"relatedItems":{"link":{"url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/itemLinks?itemId=6442d8a2d34ee8d4ade8e6db","rel":"related"}},"id":"6442d8a2d34ee8d4ade8e6db","identifiers":[{"type":"DOI","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"doi:10.5066/P9IA3TUS"}],"title":"United States Large-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database - Legacy Versions (ver. 1.0 - ver. 3.0)","summary":"This data provides locations and technical specifications of legacy versions (ver. 1.0 - ver. X.X) of the United States Large-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database.  Each release, typically done yearly, updates the database with newly EIA reported facilities, removes ones that were identified as dismantled, and applies other verifications based on updated imagery and ongoing quality-control. Analysts from the US Geological Survey and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory collaborated to develop and release the United States Large Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database (USPVDB). This effort built from the expertise gained while developing the regularly updated United States Wind Turbine Database (USWTDB). Starting from Energy Information Administration [...]","body":"<p>This data provides locations and technical specifications of legacy versions (ver. 1.0 - ver. X.X) of the United States Large-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database. &nbsp;Each release, typically done yearly, updates the database with newly EIA reported facilities, removes ones that were identified as dismantled, and applies other verifications based on updated imagery and ongoing quality-control.<\/p>\n\n<p>Analysts from the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/energy-resources-program\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(51, 122, 183); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">US Geological Survey<\/a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://emp.lbl.gov/\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(51, 122, 183); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory<\/a>&nbsp;collaborated to develop and release the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://eerscmap.usgs.gov/uspvdb\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(51, 122, 183); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">United States Large Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database (USPVDB)<\/a>. This effort built from the expertise gained while developing the regularly updated&nbsp;<a href=\"https://eerscmap.usgs.gov/uswtdb/viewer/#3/37.25/-96.25\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(51, 122, 183); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">United States Wind Turbine Database (USWTDB)<\/a>. Starting from&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.eia.gov/\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(51, 122, 183); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">Energy Information Administration (EIA)<\/a>&nbsp;data, locations of LSPV facilities were visually verified using high-resolution aerial imagery; a polygon was drawn around the extent of facility panel arrays, and facility attributes were appended. Quality assurance and control were achieved via team peer review, and comparing the USPVDB to other datasets of US PV. The data are available in several formats, including an interactive web application, comma-separated value spreadsheet (CSV), application programming interface (API), and a shapefile. The data are available for use by academic researchers, engineers and developers from PV companies, government agencies, planners, educators, and the general public.<br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<div>All versions (current and legacy) are&nbsp;available for download at&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5066/P9IA3TUS\" style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline;\">https://doi.org/10.5066/P9IA3TUS<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/div>\n","citation":"Fujita, K.S., Ancona, Z.H., Kramer, L.A., Straka, M., Gautreau, T.E., Garrity, C.P., Robson, D., Diffendorfer, J.E., and Hoen, B., 2023, United States Large-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Database (ver. 4.0, April 2026): U.S. Geological Survey data release, https://doi.org/10.5066/P9IA3TUS.","purpose":"The data release has the purpose of serving the data (that can be released to the public) in a way that can be machine readable. All of the data used in the larger work is included in tables within the report itself, this 1st version of data also serves the purpose of providing the information/data used in shapefile and CSV formats.","provenance":{"dateCreated":"2023-04-21T18:40:34Z","lastUpdated":"2026-06-09T19:57:15Z"},"maintenanceUpdateFrequency":"Yearly","hasChildren":false,"parentId":"66707f69d34e89718fa3f82f","contacts":[{"name":"Louisa A Kramer","oldPartyId":60961,"type":"Point of Contact","contactType":"person","onlineResource":"https://usgs.gov/staff-profiles/louisa-kramer","email":"lkramer@usgs.gov","active":true,"firstName":"Louisa","middleName":"A","lastName":"Kramer","organization":{},"primaryLocation":{"officePhone":"3032363226","streetAddress":{},"mailAddress":{}},"orcId":"0000-0002-6776-9768"},{"name":"K. Sydny Fujita","type":"Originator","contactType":"person","organization":{},"primaryLocation":{"streetAddress":{},"mailAddress":{}}},{"name":"Zachary H Ancona","oldPartyId":59292,"type":"Originator","contactType":"person","onlineResource":"https://usgs.gov/staff-profiles/zach-ancona","email":"zancona@usgs.gov","active":true,"jobTitle":"Physcial Science Technician","firstName":"Zachary","middleName":"H","lastName":"Ancona","organization":{"displayText":"Geosciences and Environmental Change Science Center"},"primaryLocation":{"name":"Zachary H Ancona/GEOG/VOL/USGS/DOI - Primary Location","building":"DFC Bldg 25","buildingCode":"KAE","officePhone":"3032361886","faxPhone":"3032365349","streetAddress":{"line